 # Resume Session Titles
 
 - Explicit title generation in `codex resume` is independent of ordinary automatic TUI titles and `/rename` suggestions.
+- Press Ctrl+G to generate and save a title for the selected active session.
+- While generation runs, continue navigating and press Ctrl+G on other sessions to queue them in selection order.
+- Pressing Ctrl+G again on the current or an already queued session does not add another request.
+- Only explicitly selected sessions enter the queue; filtering, title pinning and arriving pages do not expand or reorder its work.
+- Only one title generation runs at a time, including its corrective retry and saved-name update. After each title completes, the next target waits at least two seconds before starting.
+- The two-second deadline remains in force when the queue becomes empty and another session is selected shortly afterward.
+- The Ctrl+G hint stays visible during navigation, distinguishes the active, queued and available sessions, and shows live current-item/total progress when multiple targets have been selected.
+- A failure identifies the affected session and continues the remaining queue after the same two-second interval.
+- Closing the picker cancels active or waiting work and discards all unstarted targets.
+- Existing names do not prevent generation.
+- The Ctrl+G hint reads generate title for an unnamed session and regenerate title for a named session.
+- During generation, the Ctrl+G description reads generating title in bold yellow only while its actual target session is selected; moving to another session does not transfer that activity highlight.
+- After successful generation, the description reads generated title in bold green until selection moves to another session.
+- Press Ctrl+R to open a manual naming dialog prefilled with the current name.
+- Enter saves the edited name without calling a model or entering the session.
+- Escape or Ctrl+C closes the naming dialog without changing the name.
+- Pending or failed title actions preserve the saved name.
 - Generation summarizes the latest 100 nonempty user and assistant messages from native paginated history.
 - Assistant commentary is included.
 - Tool results and reasoning items are excluded.
